Here's a complete single-file site — a little "comedy club" stage where each click sets up a new bit and the punchline lands a beat later, with a confetti pop.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>The Punchline Parlor</title>
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bungee&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --gold: #f5c542;
    --gold-dark: #b98a12;
    --red: #e8452c;
    --cream: #f6efe0;
    --ink: #22201a;
  }

  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    min-height: 100vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 34px;
    padding: 40px 16px 24px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, #0c1a15 0%, #10241c 55%, #0a1410 100%);
    font-family: 'Space Grotesk', sans-serif;
    color: #fff;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }

  /* ---------- stage atmosphere ---------- */
  .spot {
    position: fixed;
    top: -25%;
    left: 50%;
    width: 75vw;
    height: 130vh;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 18%, rgba(255,210,62,.13), transparent 62%);
    animation: sway 9s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  @keyframes sway { from { transform: translateX(-7%) } to { transform: translateX(7%) } }

  .dust { position: fixed; inset: 0; pointer-events: none; overflow: hidden; }
  .dust span {
    position: absolute;
    width: 5px; height: 5px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(255,210,62,.35);
    animation: drift 10s ease-in-out infinite alternate;
  }
  @keyframes drift { from { transform: translateY(0) } to { transform: translateY(-45px) } }

  .noise {
    position: fixed; inset: 0;
    background-image: url("data:image/svg+xml;utf8,<svg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' width='120' height='120'><filter id='n'><feTurbulence type='fractalNoise' baseFrequency='0.9' numOctaves='2'/></filter><rect width='120' height='120' filter='url(%23n)' opacity='0.5'/></svg>");
    opacity: .05;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 5;
  }

  /* ---------- marquee ---------- */
  .marquee {
    width: min(92vw, 640px);
    text-align: center;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .bulbs { display: flex; justify-content: center; gap: 14px; padding: 10px 0; }
  .bulb {
    width: 10px; height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--gold);
    box-shadow: 0 0 8px rgba(255,210,62,.8);
    animation: blink 1.4s infinite;
  }
  @keyframes blink {
    0%, 100% { opacity: .3; box-shadow: none; }
    50%      { opacity: 1; }
  }
  .onair {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: .24em;
    color: var(--red);
  }
  .onair i {
    width: 9px; height: 9px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--red);
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px var(--red);
    animation: blink 1.6s infinite;
  }
  .marquee h1 {
    font-family: 'Bungee', cursive;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 2.5rem);
    color: var(--gold);
    letter-spacing: .04em;
    text-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(245,197,66,.35);
    margin: 6px 0;
  }

  /* ---------- joke card ---------- */
  .card-wrap { perspective: 1000px; z-index: 2; }
  .card {
    width: min(92vw, 520px);
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink);
    padding: 38px 32px 32px;
    border-radius: 10px;
    position: relative;
    transform: rotateZ(-.6deg);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 50px rgba(0,0,0,.45);
    transition: transform .3s ease;
  }
  .tape {
    position: absolute;
    top: -13px;
    width: 92px; height: 26px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.55);
    border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 4px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
  }
  .t1 { left: 18%;  transform: rotate(-4deg); }
  .t2 { right: 16%; transform: rotate(3deg); }

  .card-head {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .label {
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: .2em;
    color: #a08c5f;
  }
  .counter {
    font-family: 'Bungee', cursive;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #b34a12;
  }

  .joke { transition: opacity .25s ease, transform .25s ease; }
  .joke.out { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(10px); }

  .setup {
    font-size: clamp(1.05rem, 3vw, 1.25rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.45;
    margin-bottom: 16px;
  }
  .punch {
    font-family: 'Bungee', cursive;
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 3.4vw, 1.45rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--red);
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(12px) scale(.95);
  }
  .punch.in { animation: pop .5s cubic-bezier(.2,.9,.3,1.35) forwards; }
  @keyframes pop {
    from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(12px) scale(.95); }
    to   { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  }

  /* ---------- button ---------- */
  .btn {
    font-family: 'Bungee', cursive;
    font-size: 1rem;
    letter-spacing: .04em;
    color: #241a05;
    background: var(--gold);
    border: none;
    border-radius: 12px;
    padding: 16px 40px;
    cursor: pointer;
    box-shadow: 0 7px 0 var(--gold-dark);
    transition: transform .12s ease, box-shadow .12s ease, filter .12s ease;
    z-index: 2;
  }
  .btn:hover { transform: translateY(-2px); box-shadow: 0 9px 0 var(--gold-dark); filter: brightness(1.05); }
  .btn:active { transform: translateY(5px); box-shadow: 0 2px 0 var(--gold-dark); }
  .btn:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid var(--gold); outline-offset: 4px; }

  /* ---------- tally ---------- */
  .tally { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; z-index: 2; }
  .tally-label { font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .22em; color: rgba(255,255,255,.45); }
  .tally-bulbs { display: flex; gap: 10px; }
  .tally-bulbs span {
    width: 10px; height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,.15);
    transition: background .3s, box-shadow .3s, transform .3s;
  }
  .tally-bulbs span.lit {
    background: var(--gold);
    box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(255,210,62,.8);
    transform: scale(1.15);
  }

  footer {
    margin-top: 18px;
    font-size: .75rem;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    color: rgba(255,255,255,.4);
    z-index: 2;
  }

  /* ---------- confetti ---------- */
  .confetti {
    position: fixed;
    width: 8px; height: 12px;
    border-radius: 2px;
    pointer-events: none;
    z-index: 10;
    animation: conf 1.1s cubic-bezier(.2,.7,.4,1) forwards;
  }
  @keyframes conf {
    to { transform: translate(var(--dx), var(--dy)) rotate(var(--rot)); opacity: 0; }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    * { animation: none !important; transition: none !important; }
    .punch { opacity: 1; transform: none; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

  <div class="spot"></div>
  <div class="dust">
    <span style="left:12%; top:20%; animation-duration:9s"></span>
    <span style="left:28%; top:65%; animation-duration:12s; animation-delay:-4s"></span>
    <span style="left:55%; top:30%; animation-duration:10s; animation-delay:-2s"></span>
    <span style="left:72%; top:70%; animation-duration:11s; animation-delay:-6s"></span>
    <span style="left:85%; top:25%; animation-duration:13s; animation-delay:-3s"></span>
    <span style="left:44%; top:80%; animation-duration:8s; animation-delay:-5s"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="noise"></div>

  <header class="marquee">
    <div class="bulbs" id="bulbs"></div>
    <div class="onair"><i></i>ON AIR</div>
    <h1>The Punchline Parlor</h1>
    <div class="bulbs" id="bulbs2"></div>
  </header>

  <main class="card-wrap">
    <div class="card" id="card">
      <div class="tape t1"></div>
      <div class="tape t2"></div>
      <div class="card-head">
        <span class="label">TONIGHT'S SET</span>
        <span class="counter" id="counter">BIT 00 / 04</span>
      </div>
      <div class="joke" id="joke" aria-live="polite">
        <p class="setup" id="setup"></p>
        <p class="punch" id="punch"></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <button class="btn" id="btn">🎤 NEXT JOKE</button>

  <div class="tally">
    <span class="tally-label">BITS TOLD</span>
    <div class="tally-bulbs" id="tally"></div>
  </div>

  <footer>4 bits in the set · no repeats until the set ends · house lights off</footer>

<script>
  const jokes = [
    { setup: "Why don't scientists trust atoms?",  punch: "Because they make up everything." },
    { setup: "I told my wife she was drawing her eyebrows too high.", punch: "She looked surprised." },
    { setup: "Why did the scarecrow win an award?", punch: "He was outstanding in his field." },
    { setup: "I'm reading a book about anti-gravity.", punch: "It's impossible to put down." }
  ];

  const setupEl  = document.getElementById('setup');
  const punchEl  = document.getElementById('punch');
  const jokeEl   = document.getElementById('joke');
  const counterEl= document.getElementById('counter');
  const btn      = document.getElementById('btn');
  const card     = document.getElementById('card');
  const tallyEl  = document.getElementById('tally');

  const reduced = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)').matches;
  let prev = -1, told = 0, busy = false;

  // Marquee bulbs
  ['bulbs', 'bulbs2'].forEach(id => {
    const el = document.getElementById(id);
    for (let i = 0; i < 14; i++) {
      const b = document.createElement('span');
      b.className = 'bulb';
      b.style.animationDelay = (i * 0.12) + 's';
      el.appendChild(b);
    }
  });

  // Tally bulbs
  for (let i = 0; i < 4; i++) tallyEl.appendChild(document.createElement('span'));

  function pad(n) { return String(n).padStart(2, '0'); }

  function pick() {
    let i;
    do { i = Math.floor(Math.random() * jokes.length); }
    while (i === prev && jokes.length > 1);
    return i;
  }

  function confetti() {
    if (reduced) return;
    const r = card.getBoundingClientRect();
    const cx = r.left + r.width / 2, cy = r.top + r.height / 2;
    const colors = ['#f5c542', '#e8452c', '#f6efe0', '#3fb9a0'];
    for (let k = 0; k < 26; k++) {
      const c = document.createElement('div');
      c.className = 'confetti';
      const a = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;
      const d = 90 + Math.random() * 140;
      c.style.left = (cx + Math.cos(a) * d) + 'px';
      c.style.top  = (cy + Math.sin(a) * d) + 'px';
      c.style.background = colors[k % colors.length];
      c.style.setProperty('--dx',  (Math.cos(a) * d * .9).toFixed(0) + 'px');
      c.style.setProperty('--dy',  (Math.sin(a) * d * .9 + 60).toFixed(0) + 'px');
      c.style.setProperty('--rot', (Math.random() * 720 - 360).toFixed(0) + 'deg');
      document.body.appendChild(c);
      setTimeout(() => c.remove(), 1200);
    }
  }

  function next() {
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    const i = pick();
    told++;
    prev = i;

    counterEl.textContent = 'BIT ' + pad(told) + ' / 04';
    const litCount = told % 4 || 4;
    [...tallyEl.children].forEach((dot, k) => dot.classList.toggle('lit', k < litCount));

    jokeEl.classList.add('out');
    setTimeout(() => {
      setupEl.textContent = jokes[i].setup;
      punchEl.textContent = jokes[i].punch;
      punchEl.classList.remove('in');
      void punchEl.offsetWidth; // restart the pop animation
      jokeEl.classList.remove('out');
      setTimeout(() => {
        punchEl.classList.add('in');
        confetti();
        busy = false;
      }, reduced ? 0 : 700);
    }, reduced ? 0 : 240);
  }

  btn.addEventListener('click', next);
  setTimeout(next, 400); // open with the first bit

  // Gentle card tilt
  card.addEventListener('mousemove', e => {
    if (reduced) return;
    const r = card.getBoundingClientRect();
    const x = (e.clientX - r.left) / r.width - .5;
    const y = (e.clientY - r.top) / r.height - .5;
    card.style.transform = 'rotateY(' + (x * 7) + 'deg) rotateX(' + (-y * 7) + 'deg) rotateZ(-.6deg)';
  });
  card.addEventListener('mouseleave', () => card.style.transform = '');
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

**How it works:**
- **The joke list** lives in the `jokes` array at the top of the script — swap in your own four (or more) jokes there.
- **Random pick** always avoids repeating the joke you just heard.
- **Comedic timing:** the setup appears first, then the punchline pops in ~0.7s later with a confetti burst.
- **Extras:** a "bits told" tally that lights up and resets after four, a card that tilts under your cursor, and a `prefers-reduced-motion` fallback so everything still works for users who disable animations.

Just save it as `index.html` and open it in a browser — no dependencies beyond the two Google Fonts.

reasoning:
The user wants a simple HTML website: click a button → display a random joke from a list of 4 jokes. Simple, but I want to make it feel crafted and lively.

Let me think about the design. Joke site — what's the distinctive opening? Not a generic hero. A joke card, a "comedy club" vibe, or a punchline reveal with a typewriter/flip effect.

Design direction: comedy club / stand-up stage vibe. Dark stage? Or a bright, playful "joke card" aesthetic. Let me think of something distinctive:

Option A: "Comedy club" — dark stage, marquee lights, spotlight on the joke card, button like a "next bit" mic.
Option B: Bright, playful "joke card" — like a physical punchline card, bold typography, confetti on reveal.
Option C: Retro "punchline machine" — like a slot machine / typewriter.

I like the comedy club marquee idea: dark stage, warm spotlight, marquee bulbs, joke card like a stage sign. But dark + neon can feel overdone. Let me do a warm stage: deep green/charcoal stage, warm amber marquee bulbs, cream-colored joke card like a stage sign.

Actually, let me think about a different angle: "The Punchline Machine" — a playful, mechanical, bright design. Bold display typeface (like a chunky slab or retro typeface), a card that flips or slides in with the joke, a "next joke" button with a satisfying press animation, a counter of jokes told, confetti burst on reveal.

Let me pick: a bright, warm, playful "joke machine" — like a vintage punchline dispenser. Colors: warm paper cream? Cream + beige + terracotta + serif feels overdone. Let me avoid that.

Alternative: bold saturated palette — electric blue background? Or a "comedy club" deep teal/green stage with warm gold marquee. That's distinctive and not overdone.

Let me design:

- Background: deep stage green/ink (around #101820, or deep teal #0d2b2b), with a subtle spotlight gradient, faint noise, and floating "dust" particles.
- Top: marquee sign "THE PUNCHLINE PARLOR" with blinking marquee bulbs (CSS animation).
- Center: joke card — like a stage sign / ticket. Cream card with bold display typeface. Joke text appears with a staggered reveal (typewriter or word-by-word slide).
- Button: big "NEXT JOKE" button, like a stage light switch / mic button, with press animation, and confetti burst on click.
- Counter: "Joke #3 of 4" or a "bits told" tally.
- Avoid repeating the same joke twice in a row.
- Micro-interactions: button hover glow, card tilt on hover, marquee bulb blink, confetti.

Typography: distinctive display + readable body. Google Fonts: display "Bungee" or "Archivo Black" or "Fraunces"? For comedy: "Bungee" is very marquee-like. Body: "Space Grotesk" or "Karla" or "Public Sans". Let me use "Bungee" for display (marquee sign) and "Karla" or "Space Grotesk" for body. Bungee + Space Grotesk is a good combo.

Actually, for the joke text itself, a big bold serif might be funnier — like a stage sign. But Bungee for the joke text might be too heavy for long jokes. Let me use a strong display for the punchline. Let me pick 4 jokes:

1. "Why don't scientists trust atoms? Because they make up everything."
2. "I told my wife she was drawing her eyebrows too high. She looked surprised."
3. "Why did the scarecrow win an award? He was outstanding in his field."
4. "I'm reading a book about anti-gravity. It's impossible to put down."

These are classic, short, and work well.

Structure:
- Marquee header with bulbs
- Joke card: "BIT NO. 03" label, joke text (setup + punchline, punchline revealed after a delay for comedic timing — nice touch: setup appears, then "…", then punchline slides in after ~700ms)
- Button: "NEXT JOKE" with a mic icon or arrow
- Footer: small note "4 bits in the set. No repeats until the set ends."
- Confetti on reveal.

Comedic timing: when the button is clicked, the card content resets, the setup types/slides in, then after a delay the punchline pops in with a small shake or scale. That's a nice lively detail.

Implementation details:
- Single HTML file with embedded CSS and JS.
- Random: pick an index different from the previous one.
- Card: use a container; on new joke, fade out, swap text, animate in.
- Punchline reveal: separate element, hidden, shown after a timeout with a pop animation.
- Confetti: generate small divs with random colors/positions, animate with CSS keyframes, remove after animation.
- Marquee bulbs: a row of dots with staggered blink animation.
- Spotlight: radial gradient behind the card, subtly animated (slow pulse).
- Background: subtle noise via SVG data URI, plus a few floating "dust" particles.
- Button: chunky, with a shadow, press effect (translate + shadow shrink), hover glow.
- Counter: "BIT 02 / 04" with a small tally of "bits told".

Also add a subtle tilt on the card (perspective transform on mousemove) — a nice micro-interaction. Keep it simple.

Accessibility: aria-live on the joke area, focus styles, prefers-reduced-motion.

Layout: not a centered hero trio — it's a single-column stage, but that's fine because it's a joke machine; the marquee at the top, the card, the button, the footer. To make it less generic, add side elements: a "stage floor" reflection, a small "ON AIR" light, a ticket stub in the corner? Keep it tasteful.

